{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00862",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.21,
      "end_seconds": 16.68,
      "duration_seconds": 15.47,
      "text": "Hello, doctor. I'm sorry, this is rather embarrassing. I've been leaking urine. Mainly when I cough or sneeze, but also when I can't get to the toilet in time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 19.64,
      "end_seconds": 29.7,
      "duration_seconds": 10.06,
      "text": "Please don't be embarrassed, it's very common, and very treatable. How long has this been happening?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 32.28,
      "end_seconds": 43.76,
      "duration_seconds": 11.48,
      "text": "Oh, I really couldn't say. It's crept up. A year? Two? I only noticed when I had to start wearing pads."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 44.61,
      "end_seconds": 47.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "How often do you leak?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 50.36,
      "end_seconds": 63.68,
      "duration_seconds": 13.32,
      "text": "Most days. A few drops on a cough. And if I get the urge, I have to run, and sometimes I don't make it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 66.26,
      "end_seconds": 73.89,
      "duration_seconds": 7.63,
      "text": "How often do you pass urine in a day, and at night?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 75.54,
      "end_seconds": 81.27,
      "duration_seconds": 5.73,
      "text": "Eight, nine times in the day. And twice at night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 83.94,
      "end_seconds": 88.74,
      "duration_seconds": 4.8,
      "text": "Any burning, or blood in the urine? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 89.89,
      "end_seconds": 93.11,
      "duration_seconds": 3.22,
      "text": "No. None of that. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 93.98,
      "end_seconds": 97.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.36,
      "text": "What tablets are you taking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 98.69,
      "end_seconds": 111.63,
      "duration_seconds": 12.94,
      "text": "Furosemide, 40 mg, in the morning, for my ankles. A blood pressure tablet, I couldn't tell you the name, it's a little pink one. And a vitamin."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 114.43,
      "end_seconds": 125.06,
      "duration_seconds": 10.63,
      "text": "So the water tablet is 40 mg in the morning, and the pink blood-pressure tablet you can't name. What's the vitamin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 127.35,
      "end_seconds": 133.27,
      "duration_seconds": 5.92,
      "text": "Vitamin D, I think, 800 units, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 133.97,
      "end_seconds": 137.37,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "Thank you. Any other conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 140.33,
      "end_seconds": 145.67,
      "duration_seconds": 5.34,
      "text": "High blood pressure, and I've had four children."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 148.0,
      "end_seconds": 156.7,
      "duration_seconds": 8.7,
      "text": "Do you drink a lot of tea or coffee, or take any fizzy drinks? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 158.56,
      "end_seconds": 166.96,
      "duration_seconds": 8.4,
      "text": "Four cups of tea in the morning, and I like a fizzy orange. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 168.44,
      "end_seconds": 179.6,
      "duration_seconds": 11.16,
      "text": "That could be adding to it. Let me ask a few more questions. Do you ever feel that your bladder hasn't emptied? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 181.7,
      "end_seconds": 185.33,
      "duration_seconds": 3.63,
      "text": "Sometimes. I'm up and down. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 188.18,
      "end_seconds": 190.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "And any constipation? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 193.5,
      "end_seconds": 196.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "Now and then. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 198.76,
      "end_seconds": 207.56,
      "duration_seconds": 8.8,
      "text": "I'd like to check your urine today with a dipstick, to rule out infection. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 209.65,
      "end_seconds": 211.42,
      "duration_seconds": 1.77,
      "text": "Fine. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 212.24,
      "end_seconds": 228.3,
      "duration_seconds": 16.06,
      "text": "I'd say what you describe, leaking on coughing and sneezing, and also an urgent need to go that you sometimes can't hold, is a mixture of stress and urge incontinence."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 229.54,
      "end_seconds": 231.44,
      "duration_seconds": 1.9,
      "text": "Two kinds? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.06,
      "end_seconds": 239.98,
      "duration_seconds": 6.92,
      "text": "It's very common to have both, especially after childbirth and with age. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 240.85,
      "end_seconds": 243.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "What can be done? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 246.94,
      "end_seconds": 258.7,
      "duration_seconds": 11.76,
      "text": "First, pelvic floor exercises, squeezing the muscles you'd use to stop passing wind or urine, ten squeezes, three times a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 259.64,
      "end_seconds": 262.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.33,
      "text": "I've heard of those. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 263.7,
      "end_seconds": 275.67,
      "duration_seconds": 11.97,
      "text": "They work for most people if done regularly for three months. I'll also refer you to the continence physiotherapist, who will teach you properly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 277.71,
      "end_seconds": 279.38,
      "duration_seconds": 1.67,
      "text": "Right. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 281.7,
      "end_seconds": 293.99,
      "duration_seconds": 12.29,
      "text": "Cut down the tea, coffee and fizzy drinks, and don't drink too much in the evening. Keep a bladder diary for three days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 295.68,
      "end_seconds": 298.87,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "What do I write? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 299.59,
      "end_seconds": 308.43,
      "duration_seconds": 8.84,
      "text": "When you drink, what, how much, and when you pass urine, and any leaks. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 309.2,
      "end_seconds": 312.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "I can do that. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 313.37,
      "end_seconds": 320.02,
      "duration_seconds": 6.65,
      "text": "I'd like to see you again in six weeks, with the diary."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 322.14,
      "end_seconds": 325.71,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "Six weeks. Thank you. ~"
    }
  ]
}
